-- Behaviour-oriented concurrency (Cheeseman et al., OOPSLA 2023), on
-- std.domain: a cown holds a value; `when c body` spawns a behaviour,
-- which later, once, with every cown of `c` its own at once, is given
-- what they hold and gives back what they are to hold after it.
-- Behaviours whose cowns overlap run one after another, in the order
-- they were spawned; the others run at once, on as many domains as the
-- machine has cores.  A behaviour takes its cowns all at once, never
-- one and then another, so behaviours do not deadlock on them.  Import
-- it by a name, `import boc as BOC`.
--
-- > [!CAUTION]
-- > Unstable: concurrency in heff is not settled. What this module offers
-- > may change, or go, in any release.
--
-- ```haskell
-- import boc as BOC
-- import co
-- import custodian as Custodian
-- import std.domain as Domain
--
-- -- | `n` moved from one account to the other: one behaviour on both
-- paid : {e w : HFunctor}
--      -> {{bc : BOC.boc w <: e}}
--      -> BOC.Cown w Int
--      -> BOC.Cown w Int
--      -> Int
--      -> Co e Unit
-- paid from to n = do
--   with x := from
--        y := to do
--     x := x - n
--     y := y + n
--
-- -- | alice given 10, then 5 paid to bob; what bob has then, written
-- -- | by a last behaviour on bob, which comes after the others on him
-- bobs : {e w : HFunctor}
--      -> {{bc : BOC.boc w <: e}}
--      -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: e}}
--      -> {{dw : Domain.domain <: w}}
--      -> Co e (Domain.Atomic Int)
-- bobs = do
--   alice <- BOC.newCown 0
--   bob <- BOC.newCown 0
--   with a := alice do
--     a := a + 10
--   paid alice bob 5
--   seen <- Domain.newAtomic 0
--   with b := bob do
--     Domain.set seen b
--   pure seen
--
-- -- | the behaviours run, every one done: what bob has, 5
-- bobHas : {e : HFunctor}
--        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: e}}
--        -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: e}}
--        -> Co e Int
-- bobHas = do
--   seen <-
--     BOC.scheduled
--       (\why -> Domain.fail why)
--       (bobs (bc := _) (dm := _) (dw := _))
--   Domain.get seen
-- ```
--
-- Operation | What it does
-- --- | ---
-- `newCown v` | a cown holding `v`
-- `when c body` | a behaviour spawned on the cown `c`, or a tuple of them; this one goes on
-- `with a := c do ...` | the same, its body statements, `a` what `c` holds (more cowns, a binding each)
-- `with a := c where p do ...` | the same, its body run once `p` holds of what the cowns hold: until then, the behaviour waits for one `p` reads to be written
-- `with r := BOC.await act do ...` | `act`, of the world, run outside every behaviour; the body a behaviour once it has come to `r`; this one goes on
-- `with a := c` / `r := BOC.await act do ...` | the same, the body a behaviour on `c` once `act` has come to `r`
-- `with r := BOC.awaitFirst a b do ...` | `a` and `b` raced: the body once the first has come to its value, `r` `Left` or `Right` it, the other given up
-- `scheduled failed c` | `c` and its behaviours run, on domains, every behaviour waited for; `failed why` where one fails
-- `scheduledWithReactor failed c` | the same, each domain running acts awaited in a reactor of its own, every act waited for too
-- `scheduled (batch := n) failed c` | either, each domain running at most `n` behaviours in a row before the others ready get their turn (64 when not given)
--
-- A behaviour's body is given what its cowns hold, a tuple as the cowns
-- are (`(a, b, log)` hands it an `(x, y, l)`, nesting to the left), and
-- gives back their new contents, the same shape: `Cowns` says what a
-- cown or a tuple of them holds.  A `with` of cowns is a behaviour too,
-- each cown bound to a name (`with x := from` and `y := to` under it),
-- its statements the body, the names what they hold, set to change it:
-- only the cowns whose names it sets are written back, and the `with`
-- comes to `()`.  A `with` of cowns with a condition, `with a := c
-- where p do ...`, is a behaviour that, once it has its cowns, checks
-- `p` of what they hold: where it does not hold, the behaviour lets go
-- of them, untouched, and waits until a behaviour writes a cown whose
-- name `p` reads; then it is queued again on all of them, behind that
-- one, and checks `p` again (the paper's `whenever`).  One still
-- waiting once every other behaviour is done is dropped, its body never
-- run.  The body is a closed computation of the scheduler's
-- world, `boc w <+> w`, run on whichever domain takes it, later: none of
-- the handlers around the `when` (or the `with`) is around it -- a
-- `recover`, a state, a resource of a `with` -- so what it needs it
-- opens itself, or is given as a value.  It may spawn behaviours, on
-- its own cowns too (they run after it), and do what else the
-- scheduler's world allows, whose providers must then be safe on
-- threads.
-- A body that waits holds its cowns while it waits, and every behaviour
-- behind it on them waits too: what it would wait for it awaits
-- instead (below).  There is no barrier: a behaviour that
-- is to come after others on a cown is spawned after them on it, and
-- `scheduled` gives main's answer once every behaviour is done.  The
-- same cown twice in one `when` is abandoned when the `when` runs.
--
-- So a behaviour runs before every behaviour spawned after it on a cown
-- they share, wherever in the source it is.  A report meant to say what
-- the cowns hold once a server is done, written as a `with` of them as
-- the server starts, runs first, before any request, and says what they
-- held then: it reads as "at the end" and is not.  What is to come after
-- the server is spawned once the server is done, in the body of the
-- `with` that runs then -- after the act that waits for the server's end
-- (`r := BOC.await (Signal.wait [Terminate])`), say -- where it comes
-- after every behaviour spawned before it on those cowns.
--
-- A behaviour is a user of a custodian, not one of its things, as a
-- cml thread is: it takes the custodian current where it is spawned --
-- `k` in a `with k := Custodian.custody do` (or `contained`), else the
-- one current where `scheduled` runs -- and its body runs with that
-- one current, so the things its `with`s hold are in its custody, and
-- the behaviours it spawns take it too.  An act awaited, and the
-- behaviour after it, take the one current at the `await`, and the act
-- is one of its things, as what a `with` holds is: under
-- `scheduledWithReactor`, where that custodian is shut down while the
-- act waits, the act is given up -- its wait taken out of the reactor,
-- what comes after it let go of -- and the behaviour after it is never
-- spawned.  So a server's `/stop` that shuts down the custody its acts
-- were awaited in -- `with k := Custodian.custody do` around them --
-- lets go of the act waiting for a signal, and the run ends.  One that
-- has come to its value is not given up: its behaviour is spawned.
-- There is no handle to give up one act: an act given a custody of its
-- own, shut down, is that.  `awaitFirst a b` does it for two: it awaits
-- both in a custody of its own, and the first to come to its value
-- shuts it down.  No shutdown stops a behaviour.  A `with` of a custodian in a body is
-- the body's, for its extent, since a behaviour runs to its end without
-- waiting.  The custodian is the one of the scheduler's world:
-- `scheduled` asks for `custodian <: w`, and a `main` that runs it
-- names `custodian` in its world.
--
-- A behaviour whose body fails -- abandons, or fails in the runtime --
-- is done with that: its cowns hold what they held, since what they
-- are to hold is written after the body (`Domain.tried` catches the
-- failure).  Then `scheduled`'s `failed`, given why, is run, a
-- computation of the world, on the behaviour's domain while the
-- behaviour still holds its cowns: one after it on them comes after
-- that.  Then the cowns are handed on as if the behaviour had ended,
-- and the other behaviours, and main, go on.  `failed` runs on
-- whichever domain a behaviour fails on, at once with the others, so
-- what it does must be safe on threads.  A `failed` that itself fails
-- is the scope's: `scheduled`, once every behaviour is done, fails as
-- the first such `failed` did, its words kept, instead of giving main's
-- answer (the others are not stopped): `\why -> Domain.fail why` makes
-- any failure of a behaviour the run's, as it came.
--
-- A behaviour runs from its start to its end and never waits on the
-- world: what it would wait for -- a connection accepted, a socket
-- read, a sleep -- it awaits, as Verona's behaviours do, by a `with`
-- whose last binding is `r := BOC.await act`.  The `with` waits for
-- nothing, and the behaviour goes on: `act`, a computation of the
-- scheduler's world `w` (no `when` in it, nor an `await`), runs outside
-- every behaviour, and once it has come to its value, the body is a
-- behaviour of its own, `r` that value -- of the scheduler's world too,
-- as a `when`'s body is, since it runs later, elsewhere.  With cowns bound before it
-- (`with x := c` and `r := BOC.await act` under it; several cowns, a
-- tuple of them to one name, `x := (c0, c1)`), it is a behaviour on
-- them, spawned only then: no cown is held while the act waits, and
-- behaviours on a cown awaiting acts come in the order their acts came
-- to their values.  What an act fails at is its value, for the body to
-- handle -- `Net.read`'s `Either NetError Bytes`, a time limit its own
-- (`Net.read (timeout := 5000) c n`); `failed` hears only a body that
-- fails.
--
-- ```haskell
-- import boc as BOC
-- import co
-- import std.duration as Duration
-- import std.time
--
-- -- | a second's sleep awaited, then 1 added to the count, by a
-- -- | behaviour on it: the count is held by none meanwhile
-- ticked : {e w : HFunctor}
--        -> {{bc : BOC.boc w <: e}}
--        -> {{clock : time <: w}}
--        -> BOC.Cown w Int
--        -> Co e Unit
-- ticked count = do
--   with n := count
--        _ := BOC.await (sleep (Duration.seconds 1)) do
--     n := n + 1
-- ```
--
-- Under `scheduledWithReactor`, each domain has a group of std.reactor's
-- of its own: an act awaited by a behaviour is started there once that
-- behaviour is done, pending there with the others while it waits, and
-- after every 64th behaviour the domain takes the acts come to their
-- values -- a look at every act pending there, which costs as many as
-- there are -- spawning the behaviours after them, which it keeps in its slot as it
-- would one a body spawned.  A domain with no behaviour to run and acts
-- pending waits in its reactor, until one comes to its value or a
-- behaviour is put among those ready.  The run ends once no behaviour
-- runs or is ready and no act is pending: a server whose listener is
-- closed ends once its connections are done.  An act awaited by main
-- is started by a behaviour on no cown, on whichever domain takes it.
-- An act that itself fails -- abandons, or fails in the runtime, not
-- an error it comes to -- is as a body that fails: `failed` is given
-- why, on the domain it ran on, the `with`'s body is never run, and
-- every other act and behaviour goes on (it held no cown, so none is
-- let go of).  Each step of an act runs under a catch for that, as a
-- body does.  Under
-- `scheduled`, an act is run where it is awaited, there and then, the
-- behaviour holding its domain and its cowns until it is done:
-- `scheduled` is for programs that await nothing.
--
-- The scheduling is the paper's, as Verona's runtime has it: each cown
-- has a queue, kept as the last request for it, and a behaviour is
-- spawned in two phases.  First it comes to the queue of each of its
-- cowns, in the order of the cowns, by swapping itself in as the last
-- request, linked behind the one before it; then each of its requests
-- is marked come, and only then may one behind it link to it.  It
-- counts the cowns it still waits for (and one more, for its spawning)
-- and runs when none is left.  When it ends, each of its requests hands
-- its cown to the one linked behind it, or, where none is, takes itself
-- out as the last.  No lock is held for any of it: a request is a cell
-- (`Domain.Atomic`) holding its link, changed by `cas`, and told from
-- the others by the cell it is.  A behaviour whose turn has come is put
-- in a queue (`Domain.Queue`) the domains running behaviours take from
-- -- unless its turn came by a behaviour running on one of those
-- domains, spawning it or ending and handing it a cown: then that
-- domain keeps it, one at a time, and runs it next itself, as the
-- paper's threads keep a batch of their own, until it has run its
-- batch in a row, when it puts the next in the queue, so the others
-- are not starved.  No domain steals from another's batch, which is one
-- behaviour; a behaviour spawned by main is put in the queue.
--
-- The batch is 64 behaviours, or what `batch` is given (`scheduled
-- (batch := 16) failed c`).  Longer batches keep a chain of behaviours
-- on one domain, its cowns' cells warm there, and go through the queue
-- -- its lock, and waking the domain that takes from it -- less often;
-- the behaviours waiting in the queue wait for them meanwhile.  On 14
-- cores, 64 chains of 5000 behaviours, each spawning the next on its
-- cown once an act it awaited came back, ran 1.17 million behaviours a
-- second on 14 domains with batches of 64, 1.02 million with 16 and
-- 0.51 million with 4.  std.http.bocserver, 256 connections on 14
-- domains, answered 92 to 93 thousand requests a second with batches of
-- 64 or 16, with a 99th percentile of 5 ms and the slowest in 9 to 15
-- ms, and 86 thousand with 4, no faster at the tail.  A shorter batch
-- lets the behaviours in the queue in sooner, at the cost of the
-- chains; worth it where one domain's chains keep many others waiting.
--
-- A behaviour is never stopped partway -- its body runs to its end,
-- holding its cowns -- so the one a domain keeps would wait for the
-- end of the body it runs, however long that goes on.  The domain
-- counts the operations of that body as it hands them on (the world's,
-- and `when` and `newCown`), and at every 256th puts the behaviour it
-- keeps in the queue, which wakes a domain waiting there to take it:
-- a behaviour kept waits for at most 256 operations of the body.  A
-- body that computes long doing none holds its domain, and the one
-- kept, until it ends; that is the program's to avoid.

module boc
  ( Cown
  , Cowns
  , instanceCownsCown
  , instanceCownsPair
  , instanceBinderCown
  , instanceBinderCowns
  , instanceBinderCownsMore
  , instanceHolderCown
  , instanceHolderCowns
  , instanceHolderCownsMore
  , instanceWaiterCown
  , instanceWaiterCowns
  , instanceWaiterCownsMore
  , Await
  , await
  , awaitFirst
  , instanceBinderAwait
  , instanceBinderCownsAwait
  , instanceHolderAwait
  , instanceHolderCownsAwait
  , boc
  , newCown
  , when
  , scheduled
  , scheduledWithReactor
  )

import co
import custodian as Custodian
import std.domain as Domain
import std.reactor as Reactor

-- Behaviours, requests and cowns
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (a worker's group of the reactor: each act started in it comes to
-- what is to run once the act has come to its value)
type Group (w : HFunctor) = Reactor.Group (Co w Unit)

-- (an act awaited, to be started: the custodian current at its await,
-- where it is not the root's, and the act, come to what is to run once
-- it has come to its value)
data Starting (w : HFunctor)
  = MkStarting (Maybe Custodian.Custodian) (Co w (Co w Unit))

-- (a worker, as the computations of the scheduler's on it see it: its
-- slot, for the behaviour -- a `b` -- it is to run next, where one is;
-- how many operations the body it runs may still do before the slot
-- is let out; and, where the scheduler waits on the world through the
-- reactor, its group there, opened on its domain, each of whose acts
-- comes to what is to run once it has come to its value; the acts
-- awaited by the behaviour it runs, to be started in the group after
-- it, the last first; whether it waits in the reactor, to be woken
-- there; how many behaviours it has run since it last looked at its
-- group's acts finished; and how many behaviours and acts have ended on
-- it that the scheduler's `live` still counts.  Cells only that worker
-- touches, but its group and whether it waits, which others read under
-- the scheduler's mutex to wake it)
type Worker (w : HFunctor) (b : Type) =
  { slot : Domain.Atomic (Maybe b)
  , fuel : Domain.Atomic Int
  , starting : Domain.Atomic (List (Starting w))
  , group : Domain.Atomic (Maybe (Group w))
  , polling : Domain.Atomic Bool
  , turns : Domain.Atomic Int
  , ended : Domain.Atomic Int
  }

-- (the reactor's operations, its evidence given: where the scheduler
-- waits on the world through it.  `startIn` starts an act in a custody,
-- one of its things: in a group of its own within the worker's, which
-- the custody's shutdown gives up)
type Outside (w : HFunctor) =
  { open : (String -> Co w Unit) -> Co w (Group w)
  , start : Group w -> Co w (Co w Unit) -> Co w (Maybe (Co w Unit))
  , startIn :
        Custodian.Custodian
        -> Group w
        -> Co w (Co w Unit)
        -> Co w (Maybe (Co w Unit))
  , finished : Group w -> Bool -> Co w (List (Co w Unit))
  , pending : Group w -> Co w Int
  , close : Group w -> Co w Unit
  , wake : Group w -> Co w Unit
  }

-- (what the domains running behaviours share: the next cown's number;
-- how many behaviours are not yet done, and acts not yet come to their
-- values, main's own run one of them; what is run where a body fails,
-- and how many times that failed too; those ready, which the domains
-- take from, `Nothing` telling a domain to stop; and where the last
-- behaviour done says so, once, for `scheduled` to wait on.  Where the
-- scheduler waits on the world through the reactor, its operations;
-- and, as a domain waiting there cannot wait on a queue too, those
-- ready are kept apart instead, under a mutex -- a queue, its front and
-- its back reversed -- the domains with nothing to do waiting on a
-- condition, counted, or in the reactor, where they have acts pending,
-- counted too; whether the domains are to stop; and the workers, for
-- those waiting in the reactor to be woken; and how many behaviours a
-- domain runs in a row from its slot, its batch, before it puts the
-- next among those ready.  Of the behaviours `b`:
-- each worker holds a copy of its own, made on its domain, and a
-- behaviour is run with the copy of the worker running it, so that no
-- record of it is counted by every domain at once)
type Scheduler (w : HFunctor) (b : Type) =
  { numbers : Domain.Atomic Int
  , live : Domain.Atomic Int
  , failed : String -> Co w Unit
  , unreported : Domain.Atomic (Maybe String)
  , ready : Domain.Queue (Maybe b)
  , done : Domain.Queue Unit
  , outside : Maybe (Outside w)
  , mutex : Domain.Mutex
  , work : Domain.Condition
  , waiting : Domain.Atomic (Pair (List b) (List b))
  , idle : Domain.Atomic Int
  , polling : Domain.Atomic Int
  , stopping : Domain.Atomic Bool
  , workers : List (Worker w b)
  , batch : Int
  }

-- (a behaviour spawned: how many of its cowns it still waits for, and
-- one more until its spawning is done; and its turn, given the
-- scheduler as the domain it runs on holds it, and that domain -- a
-- worker, or nothing, for main, which runs none)
data Behaviour (w : HFunctor)
  = MkBehaviour (Domain.Atomic Int) (Scheduler w (Behaviour w)
                                     -> Maybe (Worker w (Behaviour w))
                                     -> Co w Unit)

-- (the scheduler's state, as a domain holds it)
type Sched (w : HFunctor) = Scheduler w (Behaviour w)

-- (the domain a computation of the scheduler's runs on: a worker, or
-- main, with neither)
type Runner (w : HFunctor) = Maybe (Worker w (Behaviour w))

-- (what a request holds -- a behaviour's request for one cown is a
-- cell holding its link: it has not come to all its cowns' queues yet;
-- it has, and none is linked behind it; or the behaviour linked behind
-- it.  `NoRequest` is held by the one cell a cown's queue keeps as its
-- last while no behaviour waits for it, which no behaviour's request
-- is)
data Link (w : HFunctor)
  = NotCome
  | Come
  | Behind (Behaviour w)
  | NoRequest

-- (a request: compared only as the cell it is, never rebuilt)
type Request (w : HFunctor) = Domain.Atomic (Link w)

-- (a behaviour let go of, its condition not holding: spawned again,
-- given the scheduler as the domain spawning it holds it)
type Again (w : HFunctor) = Sched w -> Runner w -> Co w Unit

-- (a cown, as its queue: its number, which orders the cowns of a
-- behaviour; the last request for it; the request it keeps as the
-- last while no behaviour waits for it; and the behaviours waiting for
-- it to be written, their conditions reading it -- held, as what it
-- holds is, only by the behaviour that has the cown)
data Handle (w : HFunctor)
  = MkHandle Int (Domain.Atomic (Request w)) (Request w) (Domain.Atomic
                                                            (List (Again w)))

-- | A cown holding an `a`, of behaviours run in the world `w`.
data Cown (w : HFunctor) a = MkCown (Handle w) (Domain.Atomic a)

handleOf : {w : HFunctor} -> {a : Type} -> Cown w a -> Handle w
handleOf (MkCown h at) = h

cellOf : {w : HFunctor} -> {a : Type} -> Cown w a -> Domain.Atomic a
cellOf (MkCown h at) = at

numberOf : {w : HFunctor} -> Handle w -> Int
numberOf (MkHandle n last none waiting) = n

waitingOf : {w : HFunctor} -> Handle w -> Domain.Atomic (List (Again w))
waitingOf (MkHandle n last none waiting) = waiting

-- (a `Bool` of a `with`'s names, the first's, or `True` where none is)
firstFlag : List Bool -> Bool
firstFlag (b :: rest) = b
firstFlag Nil = True

-- (a pair's `Bool`s a cown, `l` and `r` cowns on its sides, from a
-- `Bool` a name: the last name the whole pair's, else the first the
-- left side's and the rest, by `rest`, the right side's)
spreadPair : Int -> Int -> (List Bool -> List Bool) -> List Bool -> List Bool
spreadPair l r rest (b :: Nil) = List.replicate (l + r) b
spreadPair l r rest (b :: bs) = List.replicate l b ++ rest bs
spreadPair l r rest Nil = List.replicate (l + r) True

-- | What a behaviour can be on: a cown, or a tuple of them (`(a, b, c)`,
-- | nesting to the left); the world their behaviours run in, what they
-- | hold, how many cowns, their queues, and how what they hold is read
-- | and written -- written where its `Bool` says, one a cown, in order.
-- | `spread` makes those `Bool`s from a `with`'s, one a name: its names
-- | bound along the pairs to the right (`with a := c0`, `b := (c1,
-- | c2)` and `c := c3` binds `(c0, ((c1, c2), c3))`), the last to what
-- | is left, each name's `Bool` for every cown it holds.
theory Cowns (c : Type) where
  World : HFunctor
  Contents : Type
  width : Int
  spread : List Bool -> List Bool
  handles : c -> List (Handle World)
  read : (Domain.domain <: World) -> c -> Co World Contents
  write : (Domain.domain <: World)
        -> c
        -> List Bool
        -> Contents
        -> Co World Unit

-- | A cown: what it holds.
instance instanceCownsCown : {w : HFunctor} -> {a : Type} -> Cowns (Cown w a)
instanceCownsCown =
  { World = w
  , Contents = a
  , width = 1
  , spread = \fs -> [firstFlag fs]
  , handles = \c -> [handleOf c]
  , read = \dm c -> Domain.get (dm := dm) (cellOf c)
  , write = \dm c ws v -> case ws of
      Cons False _ -> pure MkUnit
      _ -> Domain.set (dm := dm) (cellOf c) v
  }

-- | Two (each a cown or a tuple) of one world: the pair of what they
-- | hold.
instance instanceCownsPair : {c d : Type}
                           -> {{l : Cowns c}}
                           -> {{r : Cowns d @ { World = l.World }}}
                           -> Cowns (c, d)
instanceCownsPair =
  { World = l.World
  , Contents = (l.Contents, r.Contents)
  , width = l.width + r.width
  , spread = spreadPair l.width r.width r.spread
  , handles = \p -> l.handles (fst p) ++ r.handles (snd p)
  , read = \dm p ->
        bind
          (l.read dm (fst p))
          (\x -> bind (r.read dm (snd p)) (\y -> pure (x, y)))
  , write = \dm p ws v ->
        bind
          (l.write dm (fst p) ws (fst v))
          (\u -> r.write dm (snd p) (List.drop l.width ws) (snd v))
  }

-- The effect
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- | A value of some type, the type hidden: what an operation of a type
-- | of its own holds (the effect has no parameter for it).
type Some (f : Type -> Type) = (r : Type) -> ((a : Type) -> f a -> r) -> r

-- (what it holds, changed, of whatever type)
someThen : {f g : Type -> Type}
         -> ({a : Type} -> f a -> g a)
         -> Some f
         -> Some g
someThen h s = \r use -> s r (\a v -> use a (h v))

data Making (w : HFunctor) x a = MkMaking a (Cown w a -> x)

-- (how a behaviour reads what its cowns hold, and writes it)
type Reading (w : HFunctor) t = (Domain.domain <: w) -> Co w t

type Writing (w : HFunctor) t = (Domain.domain <: w) -> t -> Co w Unit

-- (a body as a `when` hands it to the scheduler: a computation of
-- boc's world, closed -- no handler of where it was asked for is around
-- it -- written for whichever world it is put in, given where the
-- operations of `f`, boc's, and of `w`, the scheduler's world, go
-- there.  So it names boc's operations by their functor, `f`, not by
-- `boc w`, which is made of them)
type Body (f : (Type -> Type) -> Type -> Type) (w : HFunctor) t =
  (e : HFunctor)
  -> ({m : Type -> Type} -> {x : Type} -> f m x -> e.f m x)
  -> (w <: e)
  -> Co e t

-- (what a behaviour waits for: its condition, of what its cowns hold;
-- the cowns it reads, waited on where it does not hold; and those its
-- body writes, whose behaviours waiting are spawned again after it)
type Waiting (w : HFunctor) t =
  { holds : t -> Bool, reads : List (Handle w), writes : List (Handle w) }

-- (no condition, and no cown written)
unconditioned : {w : HFunctor} -> {t : Type} -> Waiting w t
unconditioned = { holds = \v -> True, reads = Nil, writes = Nil }

-- (a behaviour asked for: its cowns' queues, how what they hold is read
-- and written, what it waits for, its body -- a `b` -- and what comes
-- after the asking)
data Behaving (w : HFunctor) (b : Type -> Type) x t
  = MkBehaving (List (Handle w)) (Reading w t) (Writing w t) (Waiting w t) (t
                                                                            -> b
                                                                              t) x

makingThen : {w : HFunctor}
           -> {x y a : Type}
           -> (x -> y)
           -> Making w x a
           -> Making w y a
makingThen g (MkMaking v k) = MkMaking v (\c -> g (k c))

behavingThen : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {b : Type -> Type}
             -> {x y t : Type}
             -> (x -> y)
             -> Behaving w b x t
             -> Behaving w b y t
behavingThen g (MkBehaving hs rd wr wt body x) =
  MkBehaving hs rd wr wt body (g x)

-- (an act of the world awaited: the act, what comes once it has come
-- to its value -- a behaviour's body, a `b` -- and what comes after the
-- asking)
data Awaiting (w : HFunctor) (b : Type -> Type) x a
  = MkAwaiting (Co w a) (a -> b Unit) x

awaitingThen : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {b : Type -> Type}
             -> {x y a : Type}
             -> (x -> y)
             -> Awaiting w b x a
             -> Awaiting w b y a
awaitingThen g (MkAwaiting act k x) = MkAwaiting act k (g x)

-- (an operation of `boc`: its bodies first-order, closed computations
-- of the scheduler's world, so `m` holds none)
data BocF (w : HFunctor) (m : Type -> Type) x
  = NewCown (Some (Making w x))
  | When (Some (Behaving w (Body (BocF w) w) x))
  | Awaits (Some (Awaiting w (Body (BocF w) w) x))

-- | For behaviours on cowns, run in the world `w`: cowns made,
-- | behaviours queued on them, each run once its cowns are free, and
-- | acts of the world awaited, outside every behaviour.  A behaviour's
-- | body is a computation of the scheduler's world, `boc w <+> w`: no
-- | handler around the `when` is around it.
boc : HFunctor -> HFunctor
boc w =
  { f = BocF w
  , hfmap = \m g p -> case p of
      NewCown s -> NewCown (someThen (makingThen g) s)
      When s -> When (someThen (behavingThen g) s)
      Awaits s -> Awaits (someThen (awaitingThen g) s)
  , hmap = \m n nt p -> case p of
      NewCown s -> NewCown s
      When s -> When s
      Awaits s -> Awaits s
  }

-- (an operation of a sum put where its side's goes)
summedInto : {h k e : HFunctor} -> (h <: e) -> (k <: e) -> (h <+> k <: e)
summedInto l r (InL p) = l p
summedInto l r (InR q) = r q

-- (a computation of the scheduler's world, as a behaviour's body is
-- handed to it)
closed : {w : HFunctor} -> {t : Type} -> Co (boc w <+> w) t -> Body (BocF w) w t
closed c = \e inBoc inWorld ->
    lift (inj := summedInto (h := boc w) (k := w) (e := e) inBoc inWorld) c

-- | A cown holding `v`.
newCown : {e w : HFunctor}
        -> {a : Type}
        -> {{bc : boc w <: e}}
        -> a
        -> Co e (Cown w a)
newCown v = op (bc (NewCown (\r use -> use a (MkMaking v (\c -> c))))) val

-- (the cowns a `Bool` each says, in order: one past the `Bool`s too,
-- as `Cowns`' `write` takes them)
flagged : {w : HFunctor} -> List (Handle w) -> List Bool -> List (Handle w)
flagged (h :: hs) (False :: fs) = flagged hs fs
flagged (h :: hs) (True :: fs) = h :: flagged hs fs
flagged hs Nil = hs
flagged Nil fs = Nil

-- (a behaviour on `cs`, its body run once `ok` holds of what they hold,
-- waiting meanwhile on the cowns of the names `read` says, and writing
-- back those of the names `written` says: a `Bool` a name of a `with`,
-- spread over its cowns)
behaviourWhere : {c : Type}
               -> {e : HFunctor}
               -> c
               -> {{cw : Cowns c}}
               -> {{bc : boc cw.World <: e}}
               -> List Bool
               -> List Bool
               -> (cw.Contents -> Bool)
               -> (cw.Contents -> Co (boc cw.World <+> cw.World) cw.Contents)
               -> Co e Unit
behaviourWhere cs written read ok body =
  op
    (bc
       (When
          (\r use ->
             use
               cw.Contents
               (MkBehaving
                  (cw.handles cs)
                  (\dm -> cw.read dm cs)
                  (\dm v -> cw.write dm cs (cw.spread written) v)
                  { holds = ok
                  , reads = flagged (cw.handles cs) (cw.spread read)
                  , writes = flagged (cw.handles cs) (cw.spread written)
                  }
                  (\v -> closed (body v))
                  MkUnit))))
    val

-- (a behaviour on `cs`, writing back the cowns `written` says)
behaviour : {c : Type}
          -> {e : HFunctor}
          -> c
          -> {{cw : Cowns c}}
          -> {{bc : boc cw.World <: e}}
          -> List Bool
          -> (cw.Contents -> Co (boc cw.World <+> cw.World) cw.Contents)
          -> Co e Unit
behaviour cs written body =
  behaviourWhere cs (cw := cw) written Nil (\v -> True) body

-- | A behaviour on the cowns `cs`, one or a tuple of them, spawned;
-- | this one goes on.  Its turn comes once every behaviour spawned
-- | before it on any of them is done; then `body` is given what they
-- | hold, a tuple as `cs` is, and what it gives back is what they hold
-- | after.  The body is a computation of the scheduler's world, `boc w
-- | <+> w`, no handler around the `when` around it: what it needs, it
-- | opens itself, or is given as a value.  The same cown twice is
-- | abandoned.
when : {c : Type}
     -> {e : HFunctor}
     -> c
     -> {{cw : Cowns c}}
     -> {{bc : boc cw.World <: e}}
     -> (cw.Contents -> Co (boc cw.World <+> cw.World) cw.Contents)
     -> Co e Unit
when cs body = behaviour cs [True] body

-- | A `with` of a cown: a behaviour on it, spawned (`with a := c do
-- | ...`: `a` what it holds); this one goes on, and the `with` comes to
-- | nothing.
instance instanceBinderCown : {w : HFunctor} -> {a : Type} -> Binder (Cown w a)
instanceBinderCown =
  { Contents = \x s -> a, World = \x -> boc w <+> w, Result = \r -> Unit }

-- | A `with` of two cowns, each bound to a name (`with a := c0` and `b :=
-- | c1` under it): one behaviour on both, which takes them at once.
instance instanceBinderCowns : {w : HFunctor}
                             -> {a b : Type}
                             -> {{cw : Cowns (Cown w a, Cown w b)}}
                             -> Binder (Cown w a, Cown w b)
instanceBinderCowns =
  { Contents = \x s -> cw.Contents
  , World = \x -> boc cw.World <+> cw.World
  , Result = \r -> Unit
  }

-- | ... of more cowns (`with a := c0`, `b := c1` and `c := c2`): one
-- | behaviour on all of them, which takes them all at once.
instance instanceBinderCownsMore : {w : HFunctor}
                                 -> {a d f : Type}
                                 -> {{cw : Cowns (Cown w a, (d, f))}}
                                 -> Binder (Cown w a, (d, f))
instanceBinderCownsMore =
  { Contents = \x s -> cw.Contents
  , World = \x -> boc cw.World <+> cw.World
  , Result = \r -> Unit
  }

-- | A behaviour on a cown held by a `with`: its body's names set are
-- | what the cown holds after it; one only read is not written back.
instance instanceHolderCown : {e w : HFunctor}
                            -> {a : Type}
                            -> {{bc : boc w <: e}}
                            -> Holder
                              e
                              (Cown w a)
                              (\s -> a)
                              (\x -> boc w <+> w)
                              (\r -> Unit)
instanceHolderCown =
  { held = \c written body ->
        behaviour
          c
          written
          (\v -> bind (body (s := Unit) v) (\p -> pure (snd p)))
  }

-- | ... on two cowns.
instance instanceHolderCowns : {e w : HFunctor}
                             -> {a b : Type}
                             -> {{cw : Cowns (Cown w a, Cown w b)}}
                             -> {{bc : boc cw.World <: e}}
                             -> Holder
                               e
                               (Cown w a, Cown w b)
                               (\s -> cw.Contents)
                               (\x -> boc cw.World <+> cw.World)
                               (\r -> Unit)
instanceHolderCowns =
  { held = \c written body ->
        behaviour
          c
          (cw := cw)
          written
          (\v -> bind (body (s := Unit) v) (\p -> pure (snd p)))
  }

-- | ... on more.
instance instanceHolderCownsMore : {e w : HFunctor}
                                 -> {a d f : Type}
                                 -> {{cw : Cowns (Cown w a, (d, f))}}
                                 -> {{bc : boc cw.World <: e}}
                                 -> Holder
                                   e
                                   (Cown w a, (d, f))
                                   (\s -> cw.Contents)
                                   (\x -> boc cw.World <+> cw.World)
                                   (\r -> Unit)
instanceHolderCownsMore =
  { held = \c written body ->
        behaviour
          c
          (cw := cw)
          written
          (\v -> bind (body (s := Unit) v) (\p -> pure (snd p)))
  }

-- | A behaviour on a cown held by a `with` with a condition, `with a :=
-- | c where p do ...`: once it has the cown, `p` checked of what it
-- | holds; where it does not hold, the cown let go of, untouched, and
-- | the behaviour waits until a behaviour writes it, then is spawned
-- | again, behind that one (the paper's `whenever`).
instance instanceWaiterCown : {e w : HFunctor}
                            -> {a : Type}
                            -> {{bc : boc w <: e}}
                            -> Waiter
                              e
                              (Cown w a)
                              (\s -> a)
                              (\x -> boc w <+> w)
                              (\r -> Unit)
instanceWaiterCown =
  { heldWhere = \c written read p body ->
        behaviourWhere
          c
          written
          read
          (\v -> p (s := Unit) v)
          (\v -> bind (body (s := Unit) v) (\q -> pure (snd q)))
  }

-- | ... on two cowns: let go of both, and waiting on those `p` reads.
instance instanceWaiterCowns : {e w : HFunctor}
                             -> {a b : Type}
                             -> {{cw : Cowns (Cown w a, Cown w b)}}
                             -> {{bc : boc cw.World <: e}}
                             -> Waiter
                               e
                               (Cown w a, Cown w b)
                               (\s -> cw.Contents)
                               (\x -> boc cw.World <+> cw.World)
                               (\r -> Unit)
instanceWaiterCowns =
  { heldWhere = \c written read p body ->
        behaviourWhere
          c
          (cw := cw)
          written
          read
          (\v -> p (s := Unit) v)
          (\v -> bind (body (s := Unit) v) (\q -> pure (snd q)))
  }

-- | ... on more.
instance instanceWaiterCownsMore : {e w : HFunctor}
                                 -> {a d f : Type}
                                 -> {{cw : Cowns (Cown w a, (d, f))}}
                                 -> {{bc : boc cw.World <: e}}
                                 -> Waiter
                                   e
                                   (Cown w a, (d, f))
                                   (\s -> cw.Contents)
                                   (\x -> boc cw.World <+> cw.World)
                                   (\r -> Unit)
instanceWaiterCownsMore =
  { heldWhere = \c written read p body ->
        behaviourWhere
          c
          (cw := cw)
          written
          read
          (\v -> p (s := Unit) v)
          (\v -> bind (body (s := Unit) v) (\q -> pure (snd q)))
  }

-- Awaiting the world
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (a behaviour on no cown, spawned: `body` its work)
alone : {e w : HFunctor}
      -> {{bc : boc w <: e}}
      -> Co (boc w <+> w) Unit
      -> Co e Unit
alone body =
  op
    (bc
       (When
          (\r use ->
             use
               Unit
               (MkBehaving
                  Nil
                  (\dm -> pure MkUnit)
                  (\dm u -> pure MkUnit)
                  unconditioned
                  (\u -> closed body)
                  MkUnit))))
    val

-- | What a `with` awaits, `r := BOC.await act` or `r := BOC.awaitFirst
-- | a b`: it comes to an `a`, outside every behaviour, and the `with`'s
-- | body is a behaviour once it has.  (An act of the world `w`; or a
-- | race, which, in a behaviour of its own, awaits its acts, given what
-- | comes after the first.)
data Await (w : HFunctor) a
  = MkAwait (Co w a)
  | Raced ((a -> Co (boc w <+> w) Unit) -> Co (boc w <+> w) Unit)

-- | `act` awaited by a `with`: `with r := BOC.await act do ...`.
await : {w : HFunctor} -> {a : Type} -> Co w a -> Await w a
await act = MkAwait act

-- (the act awaited, and `k` given its value once it has come to it)
awaitedThen : {e w : HFunctor}
            -> {a : Type}
            -> {{bc : boc w <: e}}
            -> Await w a
            -> (a -> Co (boc w <+> w) Unit)
            -> Co e Unit
awaitedThen (MkAwait act) k =
  op
    (bc (Awaits (\r use -> use a (MkAwaiting act (\v -> closed (k v)) MkUnit))))
    val
awaitedThen (Raced race) k = alone (race k)

-- (an act of a race, come to its value: where it is the first to, the
-- race's custody shut down, giving up the other, and `Just` the value;
-- else `Nothing`)
firstOf : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {a : Type}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
        -> Domain.Atomic Int
        -> Custodian.Custodian
        -> Co w a
        -> Co w (Maybe a)
firstOf once race act = do
  v <- act
  n <- Domain.fetchAdd once 1
  if n == 0
  then do
    _ <- Custodian.shutdown race
    pure (Just v)
  else pure Nothing

-- (`k` given the value, where there is one)
givenJust : {e : HFunctor}
          -> {a : Type}
          -> (a -> Co e Unit)
          -> Maybe a
          -> Co e Unit
givenJust k (Just v) = k v
givenJust k Nothing = pure ()

-- | `a` and `b` awaited by a `with`, raced: `with r := BOC.awaitFirst a
-- | b do ...`, `r` `Left` what `a` came to or `Right` what `b` did,
-- | whichever came to its value first.  Both are awaited in a custody of
-- | their own, under the one current; the first to come to its value
-- | shuts it down, which gives up the other, and the body is a behaviour
-- | on that one's value alone.  A time limit is a race with a sleep.
-- | Under `scheduled`, which runs each act where it is awaited, `a` is
-- | run, then `b`, and `a` comes first.
awaitFirst : {w : HFunctor}
           -> {a b : Type}
           -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
           -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
           -> Co w a
           -> Co w b
           -> Await w (Either a b)
awaitFirst l r =
  Raced (\k -> do
    race <- Custodian.make
    once <- Domain.newAtomic 0
    Custodian.custodied race (do
      awaitedThen
          (MkAwait (firstOf once race (bind l (\x -> pure (Left x)))))
          (givenJust k)
      awaitedThen
          (MkAwait (firstOf once race (bind r (\y -> pure (Right y)))))
          (givenJust k)))

-- | A `with` of an act awaited, `with r := BOC.await act do ...`: `r`
-- | what the act comes to; the `with` comes to nothing at once.
instance instanceBinderAwait : {w : HFunctor}
                             -> {a : Type}
                             -> Binder (Await w a)
instanceBinderAwait =
  { Contents = \x s -> a, World = \x -> boc w <+> w, Result = \r -> Unit }

-- | A `with` of cowns and an act awaited, the act the last binding
-- | (`with x := c` and `r := BOC.await act` under it): `x` what `c`, a
-- | cown or a tuple of them, holds, and `r` what the act comes to.
instance instanceBinderCownsAwait : {c : Type}
                                  -> {w : HFunctor}
                                  -> {a : Type}
                                  -> {{cw : Cowns c @ { World = w }}}
                                  -> Binder (c, Await w a)
instanceBinderCownsAwait =
  { Contents = \x s -> (cw.Contents, a)
  , World = \x -> boc w <+> w
  , Result = \r -> Unit
  }

-- | An act awaited by a `with`: the act run outside every behaviour,
-- | and once it has come to its value, the body a behaviour on no cown,
-- | given it.  The behaviour asking goes on at once.
instance instanceHolderAwait : {e w : HFunctor}
                             -> {a : Type}
                             -> {{bc : boc w <: e}}
                             -> Holder
                               e
                               (Await w a)
                               (\s -> a)
                               (\x -> boc w <+> w)
                               (\r -> Unit)
instanceHolderAwait =
  { held = \aw written body ->
        awaitedThen
          aw
          (\v -> alone (bind (body (s := Unit) v) (\p -> pure MkUnit)))
  }

-- | ... and with cowns: once the act has come to its value, the body a
-- | behaviour on them, spawned then -- so behaviours on a cown are in
-- | the order their acts came to their values -- its names set what
-- | they hold after it, as a `with` of the cowns alone.
instance instanceHolderCownsAwait : {e w : HFunctor}
                                  -> {c a : Type}
                                  -> {{cw : Cowns c @ { World = w }}}
                                  -> {{bc : boc w <: e}}
                                  -> Holder
                                    e
                                    (c, Await w a)
                                    (\s -> (cw.Contents, a))
                                    (\x -> boc w <+> w)
                                    (\r -> Unit)
instanceHolderCownsAwait =
  { held = \p written body ->
        awaitedThen
          (snd p)
          (\v ->
             behaviour
               (fst p)
               [firstFlag written]
               (\t ->
                  bind (body (s := Unit) (t, v)) (\q -> pure (fst (snd q)))))
  }

-- The scheduler
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (how many operations a body does, on a worker, before the worker
-- lets its slot out: puts the behaviour in it among those ready)
fuelLimit : Int
fuelLimit = 256

-- (a worker waiting in the reactor woken, the first found, the mutex
-- held: for a behaviour put among those ready where no domain waits on
-- the condition)
wokenPolling : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
             -> Outside w
             -> List (Worker w (Behaviour w))
             -> Co w Unit
wokenPolling o Nil = pure ()
wokenPolling o (worker :: rest) = do
  p <- Domain.get worker.polling
  g <- Domain.get worker.group
  case g of
    Just grp -> if p then o.wake grp else wokenPolling o rest
    Nothing -> wokenPolling o rest

-- (every worker waiting in the reactor woken, the mutex held: the
-- domains to stop)
wokenAllPolling : {w : HFunctor}
                -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
                -> Outside w
                -> List (Worker w (Behaviour w))
                -> Co w Unit
wokenAllPolling o Nil = pure ()
wokenAllPolling o (worker :: rest) = do
  p <- Domain.get worker.polling
  g <- Domain.get worker.group
  case g of
    Just grp -> if p then o.wake grp else pure ()
    Nothing -> pure ()
  wokenAllPolling o rest

-- (`b` put among those ready, for any domain to take: where the
-- scheduler waits on the world through the reactor, at the back of
-- the queue, a domain waiting on the condition woken, or else one
-- waiting in the reactor)
readied : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Behaviour w
        -> Co w Unit
readied st b = case st.outside of
  Nothing -> Domain.put st.ready (Just b)
  Just o -> do
    Domain.lock st.mutex
    q <- Domain.get st.waiting
    Domain.set st.waiting (MkPair (fst q) (b :: snd q))
    idle <- Domain.get st.idle
    if idle > 0 then Domain.signal st.work
    else do
      p <- Domain.get st.polling
      if p > 0 then wokenPolling o st.workers else pure ()
    Domain.unlock st.mutex

-- (the first behaviour of the queue, the mutex held, if one is)
dequeued : {w : HFunctor}
         -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
         -> Sched w
         -> Co w (Maybe (Behaviour w))
dequeued st = do
  q <- Domain.get st.waiting
  case q of
    MkPair (b :: front) back -> do
      Domain.set st.waiting (MkPair front back)
      pure (Just b)
    MkPair Nil Nil -> pure Nothing
    MkPair Nil back -> do
      Domain.set st.waiting (MkPair (List.reverse back) Nil)
      dequeued st

-- (`b`'s turn come, on `runner`: kept in the worker's slot where it is
-- a worker's and the slot is empty, else put among those ready)
ready : {w : HFunctor}
      -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
      -> Sched w
      -> Runner w
      -> Behaviour w
      -> Co w Unit
ready st Nothing b = readied st b
ready st (Just worker) b = do
  kept <- Domain.get worker.slot
  case kept of
    Nothing -> Domain.set worker.slot (Just b)
    Just k -> readied st b

-- (one operation of the body on `runner` charged to its fuel: on a
-- worker whose body has used its fuel, the behaviour in the slot, where
-- one is, put among those ready, which wakes a domain waiting for one,
-- and the fuel filled again)
charged : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Runner w
        -> Co w Unit
charged st Nothing = pure ()
charged st (Just worker) = do
  left <- Domain.fetchAdd worker.fuel (0 - 1)
  if left > 1 then pure ()
  else do
    Domain.set worker.fuel fuelLimit
    kept <- Domain.get worker.slot
    case kept of
      Just b -> do
        Domain.set worker.slot (Nothing : Maybe (Behaviour w))
        readied st b
      Nothing -> pure ()

-- (one fewer cown, or the spawning, waited for: where none is left, its
-- turn come)
resolved : {w : HFunctor}
         -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
         -> Sched w
         -> Runner w
         -> Behaviour w
         -> Co w Unit
resolved st runner b = case b of
  MkBehaviour count turn -> do
    n <- Domain.fetchAdd count (0 - 1)
    if n == 1 then ready st runner b else pure ()

-- (the cell holds `v` now: what it held)
swapped : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {a : Type}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> Domain.Atomic a
        -> a
        -> Co w a
swapped at v = do
  old <- Domain.get at
  ok <- Domain.cas at old v
  if ok then pure old else swapped at v

-- (the request's link, waiting until its behaviour has come to all its
-- cowns' queues)
linkOnceCome : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
             -> Request w
             -> Co w (Link w)
linkOnceCome r = do
  link <- Domain.get r
  case link of
    NotCome -> linkOnceCome r
    _ -> pure link

-- (the behaviour linked behind the request, waiting until one is)
linkedBehind : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
             -> Request w
             -> Co w (Behaviour w)
linkedBehind r = do
  link <- Domain.get r
  case link of
    Behind b -> pure b
    _ -> linkedBehind r

-- (a request, as a behaviour holds it: its cown's queue, and the very
-- cell swapped in as the last, which only it takes out again)
type Held (w : HFunctor) = Pair (Handle w) (Request w)

-- (a new request for the cown)
requested : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> Handle w
          -> Co w (Held w)
requested h = do
  r <- Domain.newAtomic (NotCome : Link w)
  pure (MkPair h r)

requestedAll : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
             -> List (Handle w)
             -> Co w (List (Held w))
requestedAll Nil = pure Nil
requestedAll (h :: hs) = do
  r <- requested h
  rs <- requestedAll hs
  pure (r :: rs)

-- (the first phase: the behaviour come to each cown's queue as its last
-- request, linked behind the one before, once that one has come; where
-- none was, the cown is its at once)
queued : {w : HFunctor}
       -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
       -> Sched w
       -> Runner w
       -> Behaviour w
       -> List (Held w)
       -> Co w Unit
queued st runner b Nil = pure ()
queued st runner b (MkPair (MkHandle n last none waiting) r :: rest) = do
  prev <- swapped last r
  link <- linkOnceCome prev
  case link of
    NoRequest -> resolved st runner b
    _ -> Domain.set prev (Behind b)
  queued st runner b rest

-- (the second phase: each request marked come)
markedCome : {w : HFunctor}
           -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
           -> List (Held w)
           -> Co w Unit
markedCome Nil = pure ()
markedCome (MkPair h r :: rest) = do
  Domain.set r Come
  markedCome rest

-- (the behaviour done with the cown: handed to the one linked behind
-- it; where none is, the request taken out as the last, unless one has
-- just swapped itself in, which is then waited for to link)
released : {w : HFunctor}
         -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
         -> Sched w
         -> Runner w
         -> Held w
         -> Co w Unit
released st runner (MkPair (MkHandle n last none waiting) r) = do
  link <- Domain.get r
  case link of
    Behind b -> resolved st runner b
    _ -> do
      out <- Domain.cas last r none
      if out then pure ()
      else do
        b <- linkedBehind r
        resolved st runner b

releasedAll : {w : HFunctor}
            -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
            -> Sched w
            -> Runner w
            -> List (Held w)
            -> Co w Unit
releasedAll st runner Nil = pure ()
releasedAll st runner (r :: rs) = do
  released st runner r
  releasedAll st runner rs

-- (`n` behaviours or acts done, or main: where none is left, said
-- once, for `scheduled`)
finishedBy : {w : HFunctor}
           -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
           -> Sched w
           -> Int
           -> Co w Unit
finishedBy st n = do
  was <- Domain.fetchAdd st.live (0 - n)
  if was == n then Domain.put st.done MkUnit else pure ()

-- (main done)
finished : {w : HFunctor} -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}} -> Sched w -> Co w Unit
finished st = finishedBy st 1

-- (a behaviour or an act done, on `runner`: on a worker, counted there,
-- `live` told only once the worker has nothing to run -- so `live`
-- never counts fewer than are not done, and the domains do not all
-- change it at once for every behaviour)
finishedOn : {w : HFunctor}
           -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
           -> Sched w
           -> Runner w
           -> Co w Unit
finishedOn st Nothing = finished st
finishedOn st (Just worker) = do
  _ <- Domain.fetchAdd worker.ended 1
  pure ()

-- (a behaviour or an act begun, on `runner`: on a worker where one has
-- ended that `live` still counts, counted as that one, `live` not
-- changed)
begunOn : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Runner w
        -> Co w Unit
begunOn st Nothing = do
  _ <- Domain.fetchAdd st.live 1
  pure ()
begunOn st (Just worker) = do
  e <- Domain.get worker.ended
  if e > 0 then Domain.set worker.ended (e - 1)
  else do
    _ <- Domain.fetchAdd st.live 1
    pure ()

-- (those ended on the worker taken off `live`: before it looks for a
-- behaviour beyond its slot, or waits)
toldEnded : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> Sched w
          -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
          -> Co w Unit
toldEnded st worker = do
  e <- Domain.get worker.ended
  if e > 0
  then do
    Domain.set worker.ended 0
    finishedBy st e
  else pure ()

-- (no number twice, of numbers in order)
distinct : List Int -> Bool
distinct (a :: b :: rest) = a /= b && distinct (b :: rest)
distinct _ = True

-- (a `failed` failed, as `why` says: the first such failure kept, for
-- the run to fail with at its end)
unreportedAs : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
             -> Sched w
             -> String
             -> Co w Unit
unreportedAs st why = do
  _ <- Domain.cas st.unreported (Nothing : Maybe String) (Just why)
  pure ()

-- (each spawned again, in order)
spawnedAgain : {w : HFunctor}
             -> Sched w
             -> Runner w
             -> List (Again w)
             -> Co w Unit
spawnedAgain st runner Nil = pure ()
spawnedAgain st runner (again :: rest) = do
  again st runner
  spawnedAgain st runner rest

-- (`once` waiting on each cown)
waitingOn : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> List (Handle w)
          -> Again w
          -> Co w Unit
waitingOn Nil once = pure ()
waitingOn (h :: hs) once = do
  others <- Domain.get (waitingOf h)
  Domain.set (waitingOf h) (once :: others)
  waitingOn hs once

-- (the behaviours waiting on the cowns written spawned again, each
-- behind the one writing, which still has the cowns: in the order they
-- came to wait)
woken : {w : HFunctor}
      -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
      -> Sched w
      -> Runner w
      -> List (Handle w)
      -> Co w Unit
woken st runner Nil = pure ()
woken st runner (h :: hs) = do
  waiting <- Domain.get (waitingOf h)
  Domain.set (waitingOf h) Nil
  spawnedAgain st runner (List.reverse waiting)
  woken st runner hs

-- (a behaviour whose condition does not hold, which still has its
-- cowns: waiting on those its condition reads, to be spawned again,
-- `again`, once the first of them is written -- once, whichever)
waited : {w : HFunctor}
       -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
       -> List (Handle w)
       -> Again w
       -> Co w Unit
waited hs again = do
  armed <- Domain.newAtomic (True : Bool)
  let once : Again w = \here on -> do
    first <- Domain.cas armed True False
    if first then again here on else pure ()
  waitingOn hs once

-- (a behaviour spawned on its cowns' queues, `rd` and `wr` reading and
-- writing what they hold, `wt` what it waits for, `body` its work,
-- given the scheduler as the domain running it holds it: what they hold
-- is written after the body, by its answer, and the behaviours waiting
-- on the cowns written spawned again; a body that fails leaves them as
-- they were, and its failure is given to `failed` before they are let
-- go.  Where its condition does not hold of what they hold, the
-- behaviour lets go of them untouched and waits on those it reads, to
-- be spawned again)
spawnedOn : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {t : Type}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> Sched w
          -> Runner w
          -> List (Handle w)
          -> Reading w t
          -> Writing w t
          -> Waiting w t
          -> (t -> Sched w -> Runner w -> Co w t)
          -> Co w Unit
spawnedOn st runner hs rd wr wt body = do
  let ordered = List.sortOn (\h -> numberOf h) hs
  if not (distinct (List.map numberOf ordered)) then abandon
  else do
    begunOn st runner
    held <- requestedAll ordered
    count <- Domain.newAtomic (List.length held + 1)
    let turn : Sched w -> Runner w -> Co w Unit = \here on -> do
      v <- rd dm
      -- (the condition and the body applied when the computation
      -- tried runs, not where it is built: one that fails as it is
      -- applied fails there, caught)
      outcome <-
        Domain.tried
          (bind
             (later
                (\u ->
                   if wt.holds v
                   then bind (body v here on) (\a -> pure (Just a))
                   else pure (Nothing : Maybe t)))
             (\c -> c))
      case outcome of
        Right (Just after) -> do
          wr dm after
          woken here on wt.writes
        Right Nothing ->
          waited wt.reads (\st2 on2 -> spawnedOn st2 on2 hs rd wr wt body)
        Left why -> do
          reported <-
            Domain.tried (bind (later (\u -> here.failed why)) (\c -> c))
          case reported of
            Right u -> pure ()
            Left again -> unreportedAs here again
      releasedAll here on held
      finishedOn here on
    let b : Behaviour w = MkBehaviour count turn
    queued st runner b held
    markedCome held
    resolved st runner b

-- (a cown made)
madeCown : {w : HFunctor}
         -> {x a : Type}
         -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
         -> Sched w
         -> Making w x a
         -> Co w x
madeCown st (MkMaking v k) = do
  n <- Domain.fetchAdd st.numbers 1
  none <- Domain.newAtomic (NoRequest : Link w)
  last <- Domain.newAtomic none
  waiting <- Domain.newAtomic Nil
  cell <- Domain.newAtomic v
  pure (k (MkCown (MkHandle n last none waiting) cell))

-- (`act` awaited, from `runner`, and `k` given its value once it has
-- come to it, on that runner, and the scheduler as it holds it.  Where
-- the scheduler waits on the world through the reactor: on a worker,
-- the act kept, to be started in its group once the behaviour running
-- is done, and counted until it has come to its value; from main, a
-- behaviour on no cown spawned, to do that on a worker.  Where it does
-- not, the act run there and then)
awaited : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {a : Type}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Runner w
        -> Maybe Custodian.Custodian
        -> Co w a
        -> (a -> Sched w -> Runner w -> Co w Unit)
        -> Co w Unit
awaited st runner cust act k = case st.outside of
  Nothing -> bind act (\v -> k v st runner)
  Just o -> case runner of
    Just worker -> do
      begunOn st runner
      acts <- Domain.get worker.starting
      Domain.set
          worker.starting
          (MkStarting cust (bind act (\v -> pure (k v st runner))) :: acts)
    Nothing ->
      spawnedOn
        st
        Nothing
        Nil
        (\dm -> pure MkUnit)
        (\dm u -> pure MkUnit)
        unconditioned
        (\u here on -> awaited here on cust act k)

-- (the handler's monad, a computation given the domain it runs on, as
-- a functor)
runnerFunctor : (w : HFunctor) -> RawFunctor
runnerFunctor w =
  { f = \a -> Runner w -> Co w a
  , fmap = \g m -> \runner -> bind (m runner) (\x -> val (g x))
  }

-- (`c` run with `k` the custodian current, where there is one: a body
-- run later, elsewhere, as the custodian current where it was spawned
-- has it)
custodiedAt : {w : HFunctor}
            -> {t : Type}
            -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
            -> Maybe Custodian.Custodian
            -> Co w t
            -> Co w t
custodiedAt Nothing c = c
custodiedAt (Just k) c = Custodian.custodied k c

-- (an operation, on `runner`, charged to the body's fuel: the world's
-- own forwarded, their computations given the runner; a behaviour
-- spawned, and an act awaited and what comes after it, run with the
-- custodian current here)
bocAlg : {w : HFunctor}
       -> {x : Type}
       -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
       -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
       -> Sched w
       -> ({t : Type} -> Sched w -> Body (BocF w) w t -> Runner w -> Co w t)
       -> Runner w
       -> (boc w <+> w).f (\a -> Runner w -> Co w a) x
       -> Co w x
bocAlg st opened runner (InL (NewCown s)) = do
  charged st runner
  s (Co w x) (\a mk -> madeCown st mk)
bocAlg st opened runner (InL (When s)) = do
  charged st runner
  cust <- Custodian.current
  s (Co w x) (\t bh -> case bh of
    MkBehaving hs rd wr wt body k ->
      bind
        (spawnedOn
           st
           runner
           hs
           rd
           wr
           wt
           (\v here on -> custodiedAt cust (opened here (body v) on)))
        (\u -> pure k))
bocAlg st opened runner (InL (Awaits s)) = do
  charged st runner
  cust <- Custodian.current
  s (Co w x) (\t aw -> case aw of
    MkAwaiting act k next ->
      bind
        (awaited
           st
           runner
           cust
           (custodiedAt cust act)
           (\v here on -> custodiedAt cust (opened here (k v) on)))
        (\u -> pure next))
bocAlg st opened runner (InR q) = do
  charged st runner
  op (w.hmap (runnerFunctor w) (coFunctor w) (\m -> m runner) q) val

-- (the handler: a computation given the domain it runs on, so that a
-- body's spawning knows the worker's slot; `opened` how a body spawned
-- is run, given the scheduler as the domain running it holds it)
bocHandlerBy : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
             -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
             -> Sched w
             -> ({t : Type}
                 -> Sched w
                 -> Body (BocF w) w t
                 -> Runner w
                 -> Co w t)
             -> Handler (boc w <+> w)
bocHandlerBy st opened =
  { M = \a -> Runner w -> Co w a
  , ret = \v -> \runner -> pure v
  , bind = \m f -> \runner -> bind (m runner) (\x -> f x runner)
  , malg = \p -> \runner -> bocAlg st opened runner p
  }

-- (a body spawned, run: put in the scheduler's world, `boc w <+> w`,
-- and handled there, with the scheduler as the domain running it holds
-- it)
opening : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {t : Type}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Body (BocF w) w t
        -> Runner w
        -> Co w t
opening st b =
  handle
    (bocHandlerBy st (\here b2 -> opening here b2))
    (b (boc w <+> w) (inl (boc w) w) (inr (boc w) w))

-- (the handler, its bodies spawned run by it too)
bocHandler : {w : HFunctor}
           -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
           -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
           -> Sched w
           -> Handler (boc w <+> w)
bocHandler st = bocHandlerBy st (\here b -> opening here b)

-- (an act come to its value: what comes after it run, and the act no
-- longer counted)
resumed : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
        -> Co w Unit
        -> Co w Unit
resumed st worker k = do
  k
  finishedOn st (Just worker)

resumedAll : {w : HFunctor}
           -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
           -> Sched w
           -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
           -> List (Co w Unit)
           -> Co w Unit
resumedAll st worker Nil = pure ()
resumedAll st worker (k :: ks) = do
  resumed st worker k
  resumedAll st worker ks

-- (an act started in the group: in a custody, as one of its things)
startedIn : {w : HFunctor}
          -> Outside w
          -> Group w
          -> Starting w
          -> Co w (Maybe (Co w Unit))
startedIn o g (MkStarting Nothing act) = o.start g act
startedIn o g (MkStarting (Just c) act) = o.startIn c g act

-- (the acts given, started in the group in their order: each come to
-- its value at once resumed there)
startedEach : {w : HFunctor}
            -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
            -> Sched w
            -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
            -> Outside w
            -> Group w
            -> List (Starting w)
            -> Co w Unit
startedEach st worker o g Nil = pure ()
startedEach st worker o g (act :: acts) = do
  r <- startedIn o g act
  case r of
    Just k -> resumed st worker k
    Nothing -> pure ()
  startedEach st worker o g acts

-- (how many behaviours a worker runs between two looks at its group's
-- acts finished, not waiting: a look polls every act pending there, so
-- a domain holding many -- a server's idle connections -- would spend
-- its time looking after each behaviour; one with nothing else to run
-- looks, waiting, at once)
pollEvery : Int
pollEvery = 64

-- (after a behaviour, on its worker, where the scheduler waits on the
-- world through the reactor: the acts it awaited started in the
-- worker's group, and, every `pollEvery` behaviours, those of the group
-- finished since it last asked resumed, not waiting for one)
afterTurn : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> Sched w
          -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
          -> Co w Unit
afterTurn st worker = case st.outside of
  Nothing -> pure ()
  Just o -> do
    on <- Domain.get worker.group
    case on of
      Just g -> do
        acts <- Domain.get worker.starting
        case acts of
          Nil -> pure ()
          _ -> do
            Domain.set worker.starting (Nil : List (Starting w))
            startedEach st worker o g (List.reverse acts)
        t <- Domain.get worker.turns
        if t + 1 < pollEvery then Domain.set worker.turns (t + 1)
        else do
          Domain.set worker.turns 0
          done <- o.finished g False
          resumedAll st worker done
      Nothing -> pure ()

-- (the behaviour run on the worker, its body given the fuel in full,
-- and after it the one left in the slot, and so on, `n` run so far in a
-- row: the batch run, the next is put among those ready instead, at
-- their back)
ran : {w : HFunctor}
    -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
    -> Sched w
    -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
    -> Behaviour w
    -> Int
    -> Co w Unit
ran st worker (MkBehaviour count turn) n = do
  Domain.set worker.fuel fuelLimit
  turn st (Just worker)
  afterTurn st worker
  next <- Domain.get worker.slot
  case next of
    Just b -> do
      Domain.set worker.slot (Nothing : Maybe (Behaviour w))
      if n < st.batch then ran st worker b (n + 1) else readied st b
    Nothing -> pure ()

-- (a domain running behaviours, each ready one it takes and those left
-- in its slot after, until it is told to stop)
working : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
        -> Co w Unit
working st worker = do
  toldEnded st worker
  next <- Domain.take st.ready
  case next of
    Just b -> do
      ran st worker b 1
      working st worker
    Nothing -> pure ()

-- (the next behaviour for a worker, where the scheduler waits on the
-- world through the reactor: the one in its slot; else the first of
-- those ready; else, with acts pending in its group, waiting in the
-- reactor for one to come to its value, or to be woken -- for a
-- behaviour ready, or to stop -- and those come resumed, which may
-- fill its slot; else those of its group finished and not yet taken
-- -- an act that failed as it started, say, which no look since has
-- taken -- resumed, where there are any; else waiting on the
-- condition, counted among the domains idle.  `Nothing` once the
-- domains are to stop)
taken : {w : HFunctor}
      -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
      -> Sched w
      -> Outside w
      -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
      -> Group w
      -> Co w (Maybe (Behaviour w))
taken st o worker g = do
  kept <- Domain.get worker.slot
  case kept of
    Just b -> do
      Domain.set worker.slot (Nothing : Maybe (Behaviour w))
      pure (Just b)
    Nothing -> do
      toldEnded st worker
      Domain.lock st.mutex
      stop <- Domain.get st.stopping
      if stop
      then do
        Domain.unlock st.mutex
        pure Nothing
      else do
        first <- dequeued st
        case first of
          Just b -> do
            Domain.unlock st.mutex
            pure (Just b)
          Nothing -> do
            n <- o.pending g
            if n > 0
            then do
              Domain.set worker.polling True
              _ <- Domain.fetchAdd st.polling 1
              Domain.unlock st.mutex
              done <- o.finished g True
              resumedAll st worker done
              Domain.lock st.mutex
              Domain.set worker.polling False
              _ <- Domain.fetchAdd st.polling (0 - 1)
              Domain.unlock st.mutex
              taken st o worker g
            else do
              left <- o.finished g False
              case left of
                Nil -> do
                  _ <- Domain.fetchAdd st.idle 1
                  Domain.wait st.work st.mutex
                  _ <- Domain.fetchAdd st.idle (0 - 1)
                  Domain.unlock st.mutex
                _ -> do
                  Domain.unlock st.mutex
                  resumedAll st worker left
              taken st o worker g

-- (a domain running behaviours, where the scheduler waits on the world
-- through the reactor, each it takes and those left in its slot after,
-- until it is to stop)
serving : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Outside w
        -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
        -> Group w
        -> Co w Unit
serving st o worker g = do
  next <- taken st o worker g
  case next of
    Just b -> do
      ran st worker b 1
      serving st o worker g
    Nothing -> pure ()

-- (an act that failed, as what it comes to among its group's finished:
-- `failed` given why, as for a body that fails, and counted where that
-- fails too)
actFailed : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> Sched w
          -> String
          -> Co w Unit
actFailed st why = do
  reported <- Domain.tried (bind (later (\u -> st.failed why)) (\c -> c))
  case reported of
    Right u -> pure ()
    Left again -> unreportedAs st again

-- (a worker's group opened, on its domain, an act of it that fails
-- coming to `actFailed`; it serving, and its group closed once it
-- stops)
servingIn : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> Sched w
          -> Outside w
          -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
          -> Co w Unit
servingIn st o worker = do
  g <- o.open (\why -> actFailed st why)
  Domain.lock st.mutex
  Domain.set worker.group (Just g)
  Domain.unlock st.mutex
  serving st o worker g
  Domain.lock st.mutex
  Domain.set worker.group (Nothing : Maybe (Group w))
  Domain.unlock st.mutex
  o.close g

-- (the reactor's operations, in a record of this domain's own)
outsideHere : {w : HFunctor} -> Outside w -> Outside w
outsideHere o =
  { open = o.open
  , start = o.start
  , startIn = o.startIn
  , finished = o.finished
  , pending = o.pending
  , close = o.close
  , wake = o.wake
  }

-- (the scheduler's state in a record of this domain's own, holding
-- what the shared one holds: counted by this domain, not by all of
-- them at once, as it is handed from one of its computations to the
-- next)
heldHere : {w : HFunctor} -> Sched w -> Sched w
heldHere st =
  { numbers = st.numbers
  , live = st.live
  , failed = st.failed
  , unreported = st.unreported
  , ready = st.ready
  , done = st.done
  , outside = maybe Nothing (\o -> Just (outsideHere o)) st.outside
  , mutex = st.mutex
  , work = st.work
  , waiting = st.waiting
  , idle = st.idle
  , polling = st.polling
  , stopping = st.stopping
  , workers = st.workers
  , batch = st.batch
  }

-- (a worker, on its domain.  Where the scheduler waits on the world
-- through the reactor, a failure of the worker's own -- not of a body,
-- nor of an act, which its group finishes as `actFailed` -- fails the
-- run: `failed` given why, counted as a `failed` that failed, and
-- `scheduled` told at once that it is over, the acts pending of the
-- worker gone with it)
workingAs : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> Sched w
          -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
          -> Co w Unit
workingAs st worker = case st.outside of
  Nothing -> working st worker
  Just o -> do
    outcome <-
      Domain.tried (bind (later (\u -> servingIn st o worker)) (\c -> c))
    case outcome of
      Right u -> pure ()
      Left why -> do
        reported <- Domain.tried (bind (later (\u -> st.failed why)) (\c -> c))
        unreportedAs st why
        Domain.put st.done MkUnit

-- (a worker's cells, in a record of its domain's own)
workerHere : {w : HFunctor} -> {b : Type} -> Worker w b -> Worker w b
workerHere worker =
  { slot = worker.slot
  , fuel = worker.fuel
  , starting = worker.starting
  , group = worker.group
  , polling = worker.polling
  , turns = worker.turns
  , ended = worker.ended
  }

-- (a worker, on its domain, with the scheduler's state, and its own
-- cells, in records of its own)
workerOn : {w : HFunctor}
         -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
         -> Sched w
         -> Worker w (Behaviour w)
         -> Co w Unit
workerOn shared worker = do
  st <- later (\u -> heldHere shared)
  mine <- later (\u -> workerHere worker)
  workingAs st mine

-- (`n` workers, none on a domain yet)
workersMade : {w : HFunctor}
            -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
            -> Int
            -> Co w (List (Worker w (Behaviour w)))
workersMade n =
  if n <= 0 then pure Nil
  else do
    slot <- Domain.newAtomic (Nothing : Maybe (Behaviour w))
    fuel <- Domain.newAtomic fuelLimit
    starting <- Domain.newAtomic (Nil : List (Starting w))
    group <- Domain.newAtomic (Nothing : Maybe (Group w))
    polling <- Domain.newAtomic False
    turns <- Domain.newAtomic 0
    ended <- Domain.newAtomic 0
    rest <- workersMade (n - 1)
    pure
        ({ slot = slot
         , fuel = fuel
         , starting = starting
         , group = group
         , polling = polling
         , turns = turns
         , ended = ended
         }
         :: rest)

-- (each worker on a domain of its own, spawned in the scheduler's
-- scope)
workers : {e w : HFunctor}
        -> {s : Type}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> {{sp : Domain.scoped w <: e}}
        -> Domain.Scope s w
        -> Sched w
        -> List (Worker w (Behaviour w))
        -> Co e Unit
workers sc st Nil = pure ()
workers sc st (worker :: rest) = do
  _ <- Domain.spawn sc (workerOn st worker)
  workers sc st rest

-- (each domain told to stop, once no behaviour is left: one `Nothing`
-- a domain, whichever takes it; where the scheduler waits on the world
-- through the reactor, the domains woken where they wait, to stop)
stoppedAll : {w : HFunctor}
           -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
           -> Sched w
           -> List (Worker w (Behaviour w))
           -> Co w Unit
stoppedAll st Nil = pure ()
stoppedAll st (d :: ds) = case st.outside of
  Nothing -> do
    Domain.put st.ready (Nothing : Maybe (Behaviour w))
    stoppedAll st ds
  Just o -> do
    Domain.lock st.mutex
    Domain.set st.stopping True
    Domain.broadcast st.work
    wokenAllPolling o st.workers
    Domain.unlock st.mutex

-- (main's answer, or its failure handed on)
mainAnswered : {w : HFunctor}
             -> {a : Type}
             -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
             -> Either String a
             -> Co w a
mainAnswered (Right x) = pure x
mainAnswered (Left why) = Domain.fail why

-- (`c` run, its main, then every behaviour waited for, and each domain
-- told to stop -- where main fails too, before this fails as it did)
mainRun : {w : HFunctor}
        -> {a : Type}
        -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
        -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
        -> Sched w
        -> Co (boc w <+> w) a
        -> Co w a
mainRun st c = do
  r <- Domain.tried (handle (bocHandler st) c Nothing)
  finished st
  Domain.take st.done
  stoppedAll st st.workers
  mainAnswered r

-- (`c` and its behaviours run, waiting on the world through the
-- reactor where `outside` gives its operations)
scheduledBy : {w : HFunctor}
            -> {a : Type}
            -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
            -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
            -> Maybe (Outside w)
            -> Int
            -> (String -> Co w Unit)
            -> Co (boc w <+> w) a
            -> Co w a
scheduledBy outside batch failed c = do
  numbers <- Domain.newAtomic 0
  live <- Domain.newAtomic 1
  unreported <- Domain.newAtomic (Nothing : Maybe String)
  ready <- (Domain.newQueue : Co w (Domain.Queue (Maybe (Behaviour w))))
  done <- (Domain.newQueue : Co w (Domain.Queue Unit))
  mutex <- Domain.newMutex
  work <- Domain.newCondition
  waiting <-
    Domain.newAtomic
      (MkPair Nil Nil : Pair (List (Behaviour w)) (List (Behaviour w)))
  idle <- Domain.newAtomic 0
  polling <- Domain.newAtomic 0
  stopping <- Domain.newAtomic False
  n <- Domain.cores
  ws <- workersMade n
  let st : Sched w =
    { numbers = numbers
    , live = live
    , failed = failed
    , unreported = unreported
    , ready = ready
    , done = done
    , outside = outside
    , mutex = mutex
    , work = work
    , waiting = waiting
    , idle = idle
    , polling = polling
    , stopping = stopping
    , workers = ws
    , batch = batch
    }
  x <-
    with sc := Domain.scope do
      workers sc st ws
      lift (mainRun st c)
  k <- Domain.get unreported
  case k of
    Just why -> Domain.fail why
    Nothing -> pure x

-- | `c` and the behaviours it spawns, run on as many domains as the
-- | machine has cores (`Domain.cores`), every behaviour waited for:
-- | main's answer.  A behaviour whose body fails is done with that, its
-- | cowns holding what they held: `failed why` is run on its domain,
-- | while it still holds them, and the others go on.  Where a `failed`
-- | fails too, this fails as the first such `failed` did, once every
-- | behaviour is done, instead of giving the answer; where main fails,
-- | every behaviour is waited for, and this fails as main did.  An act awaited (`await`) is run where it is
-- | awaited, there and then, the behaviour holding its domain, and its
-- | cowns, until it is done.  A behaviour runs with the custodian
-- | current where it was spawned, `w`'s.  A domain runs at most `batch`
-- | behaviours in a row that it made ready itself before the others
-- | ready get their turn: fewer, for the others to wait less; more, for
-- | long chains of behaviours to run faster.
scheduled : {w : HFunctor}
          -> {a : Type}
          -> {batch : Int := 64}
          -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
          -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
          -> (String -> Co w Unit)
          -> Co (boc w <+> w) a
          -> Co w a
scheduled failed c = scheduledBy Nothing (max 1 batch) failed c

-- (an act started in a group of its own within `g`, which the custody
-- `k` has among its things: shut down while the act waits, the group is
-- given up, the act's continuation let go of, and `pure ()` comes in
-- its place, for the act to be counted done; come to its value, the
-- group closed before what comes after it runs)
startedInCustody : {w : HFunctor}
                 -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
                 -> {{rx : Reactor.reactor <: w}}
                 -> Custodian.Custodian
                 -> Group w
                 -> Co w (Co w Unit)
                 -> Co w (Maybe (Co w Unit))
startedInCustody k g act = do
  inner <- Reactor.openWithin g
  gv <- Reactor.giving inner (pure ())
  Custodian.custodied k (Custodian.owned gv)
  Reactor.start
      inner
      (bind act (\next -> pure (bind (Reactor.closeGiving gv) (\u -> next))))

-- | `scheduled`, each domain waiting on the world through a reactor of
-- | its own (std.reactor's, the C backend's): an act awaited (`await`)
-- | is run outside every behaviour, started in the reactor of the
-- | domain whose behaviour awaited it once that behaviour is done, and
-- | the behaviour that is to follow it spawned on that domain once it
-- | has come to its value.  A domain with no behaviour to run and acts
-- | pending waits in its reactor, until one has come to its value, or a
-- | behaviour is ready.  Every behaviour, and every act awaited, is
-- | waited for, but an act given up: one whose custodian is shut down
-- | while it waits, its `with`'s body never run.  An act that fails -- abandons, or fails in the runtime
-- | -- is as a body that fails: `failed` given why, its `with`'s body
-- | not run, the others going on.  `batch` as `scheduled`'s.
scheduledWithReactor : {w : HFunctor}
                     -> {a : Type}
                     -> {batch : Int := 64}
                     -> {{dm : Domain.domain <: w}}
                     -> {{cu : Custodian.custodian <: w}}
                     -> {{rx : Reactor.reactor <: w}}
                     -> (String -> Co w Unit)
                     -> Co (boc w <+> w) a
                     -> Co w a
scheduledWithReactor failed c =
  scheduledBy
    (Just
       { open = \f -> Reactor.open (failed := Just f)
       , start = \g m -> Reactor.start g m
       , startIn = \k g m -> startedInCustody k g m
       , finished = \g wait -> Reactor.finished g wait
       , pending = \g -> Reactor.pending g
       , close = \g -> Reactor.close g
       , wake = \g -> Reactor.wake g
       })
    (max 1 batch)
    failed
    c
